{"number":2,"title":"Polynomials","slug":"polynomials","color":"","level":"","estTime":"","description":"Class 9 IMO — Polynomials: degree and zeroes, the remainder and factor theorems, factorisation by splitting the middle term, and the standard algebraic identities.","topics":[{"title":"Degree and Zeroes of a Polynomial","concept":"<p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>What is a Polynomial?</strong></p><p class=\"eb-p\">A <strong>polynomial</strong> is an algebraic expression that contains one or more <strong>terms</strong>, where each term consists of a <strong>variable</strong> raised to a <strong>non-negative integer</strong> exponent, multiplied by a <strong>coefficient</strong> (a real number).</p><p class=\"eb-p\">The word \"polynomial\" comes from \"poly\" (many) and \"nomial\" (terms).</p><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>Key Components of a Polynomial:</strong></p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"concept-table\"><thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Definition</th><th>Example in 3x² + 2x - 5</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>**Coefficient**</td><td>The numerical factor of a term</td><td>3, 2, -5</td></tr><tr><td>**Variable**</td><td>The letter representing an unknown quantity</td><td>x</td></tr><tr><td>**Exponent**</td><td>The power to which the variable is raised</td><td>2, 1, 0</td></tr><tr><td>**Degree**</td><td>The highest exponent in the polynomial</td><td>2</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>Polynomials in One Variable:</strong></p><p class=\"eb-p\">A polynomial in one variable (say x) has the general form:</p><p class=\"eb-p\">aₙxⁿ + aₙ₋₁xⁿ⁻¹ + ... + a₁x + a₀, where aₙ, aₙ₋₁, ..., a₀ are constants (coefficients).</p><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>Types of Polynomials Based on Degree:</strong></p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"concept-table\"><thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Degree</th><th>Standard Form</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>**Linear**</td><td>1</td><td>ax + b</td><td>3x + 4, -2x + 1</td></tr><tr><td>**Quadratic**</td><td>2</td><td>ax² + bx + c</td><td>x² - 5x + 6, 2x² + 3x - 1</td></tr><tr><td>**Cubic**</td><td>3</td><td>ax³ + bx² + cx + d</td><td>x³ - 8, 2x³ + x² - x + 4</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>Types of Polynomials Based on Number of Terms:</strong></p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"concept-table\"><thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Number of Terms</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>**Binomial**</td><td>2</td><td>x + 3, 2x² - 5, 4x³ + 1</td></tr><tr><td>**Trinomial**</td><td>3</td><td>x² + 5x + 6, 3x³ - 2x² + x</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class=\"imo-visual\" style=\"margin:1rem 0\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 640 395\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:640px;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden\"><defs><linearGradient id=\"g\" x1=\"0%\" y1=\"0%\" x2=\"100%\" y2=\"100%\"><stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#eff6ff\"/><stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#dbeafe\"/></linearGradient></defs><rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"url(#bg)\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"640\" height=\"44\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Anatomy of a Polynomial</text><rect x=\"150\" y=\"60\" width=\"340\" height=\"52\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#3b82f6\" stroke-width=\"2.5\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"92\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#1e40af\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">3x⁴ − 5x² + 2x − 7</text><rect x=\"78\" y=\"60\" width=\"140\" height=\"58\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#f8fafc\" stroke=\"#7c3aed\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"148\" y=\"84\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#7c3aed\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Leading</text><text x=\"148\" y=\"102\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#7c3aed\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">coefficient: 3</text><line x1=\"160\" y1=\"113\" x2=\"148\" y2=\"118\" stroke=\"#7c3aed\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"4,3\"/><rect x=\"208\" y=\"60\" width=\"140\" height=\"58\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#f8fafc\" stroke=\"#16a34a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"278\" y=\"84\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#16a34a\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Degree (highest</text><text x=\"278\" y=\"102\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#16a34a\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">power): 4</text><line x1=\"248\" y1=\"113\" x2=\"278\" y2=\"118\" stroke=\"#16a34a\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"4,3\"/><rect x=\"263\" y=\"220\" width=\"140\" height=\"58\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#f8fafc\" stroke=\"#ea580c\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"333\" y=\"244\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#ea580c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Coefficient</text><text x=\"333\" y=\"262\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#ea580c\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">of x: 2</text><line x1=\"292\" y1=\"113\" x2=\"333\" y2=\"278\" stroke=\"#ea580c\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"4,3\"/><rect x=\"418\" y=\"60\" width=\"140\" height=\"58\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#f8fafc\" stroke=\"#dc2626\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"488\" y=\"84\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#dc2626\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Constant</text><text x=\"488\" y=\"102\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#dc2626\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">term: -7</text><line x1=\"490\" y1=\"113\" x2=\"488\" y2=\"118\" stroke=\"#dc2626\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-dasharray=\"4,3\"/><rect x=\"20\" y=\"295\" width=\"140\" height=\"80\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fee2e2\" stroke=\"#dc2626\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"90\" y=\"320\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#dc2626\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Monomial</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"340\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">1 term</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"358\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">3x²</text><rect x=\"175\" y=\"295\" width=\"140\" height=\"80\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#dcfce7\" stroke=\"#16a34a\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"245\" y=\"320\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#16a34a\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Binomial</text><text x=\"245\" y=\"340\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">2 terms</text><text x=\"245\" y=\"358\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">x+5</text><rect x=\"330\" y=\"295\" width=\"140\" height=\"80\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fef3c7\" stroke=\"#d97706\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"400\" y=\"320\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#d97706\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Trinomial</text><text x=\"400\" y=\"340\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">3 terms</text><text x=\"400\" y=\"358\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">x²+x+1</text><rect x=\"485\" y=\"295\" width=\"140\" height=\"80\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#ede9fe\" stroke=\"#7c3aed\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"555\" y=\"320\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#7c3aed\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Polynomial</text><text x=\"555\" y=\"340\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">n terms</text></svg></div>","visual":null,"examples":[{"number":"1","problem":"State the degree of 4x³ − 7x + 2.","solution":"The highest power is 3, so the degree is 3 (cubic)."},{"number":"2","problem":"Is x = 2 a zero of p(x) = x² − 5x + 6?","solution":"p(2) = 4 − 10 + 6 = 0, so yes, 2 is a zero."}],"recap":["Degree = highest power of the variable.","A zero of p(x) makes p(x) = 0; evaluate by substituting the value."],"quiz":[{"q":"If a + b + c = 9 and ab + bc + ca = 26, then the value of a² + b² + c² is:","options":["29","81","55","35"],"correct":0,"explanation":"(a + b + c)² = a² + b² + c² + 2(ab + bc + ca), so 81 = a² + b² + c² + 52, giving a² + b² + c² = 29.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"What is the zero of the linear polynomial p(x) = cx + d, where c ≠ 0?","options":["−d/c","d/c","−c/d","c/d"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Set cx + d = 0, so cx = −d and x = −d/c.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"}]},{"title":"Remainder and Factor Theorems","concept":"<p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>What is Polynomial Division?</strong></p><p class=\"eb-p\">Polynomial division is similar to long division with numbers. When dividing a polynomial by a <strong>linear divisor</strong> (x - a), we can use two methods:</p><ol class=\"concept-list\"><li><strong>Long division</strong> (general method)</li><li><strong>Synthetic division</strong> (shortcut when divisor is x - a)</li></ol><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>Division Algorithm for Polynomials:</strong></p><p class=\"eb-p\">When dividing polynomial P(x) by divisor d(x), we get:</p><div class=\"formula-block\">P(x) = d(x) × Q(x) + R(x)</div><p class=\"eb-p\">Where Q(x) is the quotient and R(x) is the remainder. The degree of R(x) is less than the degree of d(x).</p><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>What is a Zero of a Polynomial?</strong></p><p class=\"eb-p\">A <strong>zero</strong> (or root) of a polynomial P(x) is a value of x for which P(x) = 0.</p><ul class=\"concept-list\"><li>If P(a) = 0, then a is a zero of the polynomial</li><li>Geometrically, a zero means the graph of the polynomial crosses the x-axis at x = a</li></ul><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>Remainder Theorem:</strong></p><p class=\"eb-p\">When a polynomial P(x) is divided by (x - a), the remainder is P(a).</p><div class=\"formula-block\">This means: P(x) = (x - a) × Q(x) + P(a)</div><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>Factor Theorem (special case of Remainder Theorem):</strong></p><div class=\"formula-block\">If P(a) = 0, then (x - a) is a factor of P(x).</div><div class=\"imo-visual\" style=\"margin:1rem 0\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 640 375\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:640px;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden\"><defs><linearGradient id=\"g\" x1=\"0%\" y1=\"0%\" x2=\"100%\" y2=\"100%\"><stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#fdf4ff\"/><stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#fae8ff\"/></linearGradient></defs><rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"url(#bg)\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"640\" height=\"44\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#9333ea\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Remainder Theorem</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"60\" width=\"580\" height=\"50\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#f5f3ff\" stroke=\"#a78bfa\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"82\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#7c3aed\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Remainder Theorem: When p(x) is divided by (x - a),</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"100\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#7c3aed\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">the remainder is p(a)</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"125\" width=\"580\" height=\"140\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#e2e8f0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"80\" y=\"155\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Example: p(x) = x³ - 3x + 5, divide by (x - 2)</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"178\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Remainder Theorem: remainder = p(2)</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"200\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#7c3aed\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">p(2) = (2)³ - 3(2) + 5 = 8 - 6 + 5 = 7</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"215\" width=\"200\" height=\"30\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#ede9fe\" stroke=\"#7c3aed\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"180\" y=\"234\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#7c3aed\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">∴ Remainder = 7</text><text x=\"400\" y=\"155\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#64748b\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Verify by Long Division:</text><text x=\"400\" y=\"178\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">x³-3x+5 ÷ (x-2)</text><line x1=\"395\" y1=\"188\" x2=\"590\" y2=\"188\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-width=\"1\"/><text x=\"400\" y=\"205\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Quotient: x²+2x+1</text><text x=\"400\" y=\"222\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#16a34a\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Remainder: 7 ✓</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"285\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#64748b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Applications: Test divisibility, find unknown coefficients</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"295\" width=\"580\" height=\"60\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#fef3c7\" stroke=\"#fbbf24\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"318\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#92400e\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">If p(a) = 0, then (x - a) is a FACTOR of p(x)</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"340\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"#78350f\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">This is the Factor Theorem!</text></svg></div>","visual":null,"examples":[{"number":"1","problem":"Find the remainder when x³ + 1 is divided by (x + 1).","solution":"Here a = −1: p(−1) = (−1)³ + 1 = 0, so the remainder is 0."},{"number":"2","problem":"Is (x − 1) a factor of x³ − 1?","solution":"p(1) = 1 − 1 = 0, so by the Factor Theorem (x − 1) is a factor."}],"recap":["Remainder on dividing p(x) by (x − a) is p(a).","(x − a) is a factor ⟺ p(a) = 0."],"quiz":[{"q":"If (x − 2) is a factor of x² + kx + 2k, then the value of k is:","options":["−1","1","−2","2"],"correct":0,"explanation":"By the Factor Theorem p(2) = 0: 4 + 2k + 2k = 0 → 4 + 4k = 0 → k = −1.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"The expansion of (x − 2y − 3z)² is:","options":["x² + 4y² + 9z² − 4xy + 12yz − 6zx","x² + 4y² + 9z² − 4xy − 12yz − 6zx","x² − 4y² − 9z² − 4xy + 12yz − 6zx","x² + 4y² + 9z² + 4xy + 12yz + 6zx"],"correct":0,"explanation":"With a = x, b = −2y, c = −3z: squares x² + 4y² + 9z²; cross terms 2(x)(−2y) = −4xy, 2(−2y)(−3z) = +12yz, 2(−3z)(x) = −6zx.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"}]},{"title":"Factorisation and Algebraic Identities","concept":"<p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>What is Factorization?</strong></p><p class=\"eb-p\">Factorization (or factoring) is the process of writing a polynomial as a product of simpler polynomials (factors). It's the reverse of multiplication.</p><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>Key Algebraic Identities for Factorization:</strong></p><div class=\"table-scroll\"><table class=\"concept-table\"><thead><tr><th>Identity</th><th>Formula</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>**Perfect Square (Difference)**</td><td>(x - y)² = x² - 2xy + y²</td><td>(x - 5)² = x² - 10x + 25</td></tr><tr><td>**Difference of Squares**</td><td>x² - y² = (x + y)(x - y)</td><td>x² - 16 = (x + 4)(x - 4)</td></tr><tr><td>**Product of Binomials**</td><td>(x + a)(x + b) = x² + (a + b)x + ab</td><td>(x + 3)(x + 4) = x² + 7x + 12</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>Steps to Factor a Quadratic Trinomial (x² + bx + c):</strong></p><ol class=\"concept-list\"><li>Find two numbers whose <strong>product</strong> = c and <strong>sum</strong> = b</li><li>Write as (x + m)(x + n) where m × n = c and m + n = b</li></ol><p class=\"eb-p\"><strong>Special Cases:</strong></p><ul class=\"concept-list\"><li>If a ≠ 1 in ax² + bx + c, factoring requires more steps (splitting middle term)</li><li>Difference of squares: a² - b² = (a - b)(a + b)</li><li>Sum of squares a² + b² cannot be factored with real numbers</li></ul><div class=\"imo-visual\" style=\"margin:1rem 0\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 640 360\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:640px;height:auto;display:block;margin:0 auto;border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden\"><defs><linearGradient id=\"g\" x1=\"0%\" y1=\"0%\" x2=\"100%\" y2=\"100%\"><stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#fff7ed\"/><stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#ffedd5\"/></linearGradient></defs><rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"url(#bg)\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"640\" height=\"44\" rx=\"0\" fill=\"#ea580c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"28\" font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Factor Theorem &amp; Factorisation</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"58\" width=\"580\" height=\"48\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff7ed\" stroke=\"#fb923c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"78\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#7c2d12\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Factor Theorem: (x - a) is a factor of p(x) ⟺ p(a) = 0</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#9a3412\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">i.e. a is a zero (root) of the polynomial</text><rect x=\"30\" y=\"120\" width=\"580\" height=\"150\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#e2e8f0\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"320\" y=\"148\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#1e293b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Factorise: p(x) = x³ - 6x² + 11x - 6</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"172\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#15803d\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Try x=1: p(1) = 1 - 6 + 11 - 6 = 0  ✓  → (x-1) is a factor</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"194\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Divide: x³-6x²+11x-6 ÷ (x-1) = x²-5x+6</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"216\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#374151\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"normal\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Factorise x²-5x+6 = (x-2)(x-3)</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"228\" width=\"320\" height=\"30\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#dcfce7\" stroke=\"#16a34a\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"240\" y=\"247\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#15803d\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">∴ p(x) = (x-1)(x-2)(x-3)</text><text x=\"320\" y=\"282\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#1e293b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">Zeros of the polynomial: x = 1, 2, 3</text><circle cx=\"220\" cy=\"320\" r=\"20\" fill=\"#3b82f6\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"220\" y=\"325\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">x=1</text><circle cx=\"340\" cy=\"320\" r=\"20\" fill=\"#16a34a\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"340\" y=\"325\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">x=2</text><circle cx=\"460\" cy=\"320\" r=\"20\" fill=\"#ea580c\" stroke=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"460\" y=\"325\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-family=\"system-ui,sans-serif\">x=3</text></svg></div>","visual":null,"examples":[{"number":"1","problem":"Factorise x² + 7x + 12.","solution":"Split 7 as 3 + 4: x² + 3x + 4x + 12 = (x + 3)(x + 4)."},{"number":"2","problem":"Using an identity, expand (a + b + c)² when a = b = c = 1.","solution":"1 + 1 + 1 + 2(1 + 1 + 1) = 3 + 6 = 9, which is (1+1+1)² = 9."}],"recap":["Split the middle term to factorise quadratics.","Know (x+y+z)² and the x³+y³+z³−3xyz identity."],"quiz":[{"q":"If x = −1 is a zero of p(x) = kx³ − 2x² + x + 4, find k.","options":["1","−1","2","3"],"correct":0,"explanation":"p(−1) = −k − 2 − 1 + 4 = −k + 1 = 0, so k = 1.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"Find the remainder when p(x) = 2x³ − 7x² + 9x − 2 is divided by (2x − 1).","options":["1","0","2","−1"],"correct":0,"explanation":"By the Remainder Theorem put x = 1/2: p(1/2) = 2(1/8) − 7(1/4) + 9(1/2) − 2 = 1/4 − 7/4 + 18/4 − 8/4 = 4/4 = 1.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"}]}],"tests":{"online":{"title":"","minutes":20,"questions":[{"q":"If x + y + z = 0, then the value of x²/yz + y²/zx + z²/xy is:","options":["3","0","1","−3"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Taking the common denominator xyz gives (x³ + y³ + z³)/xyz. Since x + y + z = 0, x³ + y³ + z³ = 3xyz, so the value is 3xyz/xyz = 3.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"Statement A: A binomial can have degree 100. Statement B: A polynomial of degree 1 can have 3 terms. Which is true?","options":["Only A","Only B","Both A and B","Neither A nor B"],"correct":0,"explanation":"A is true (e.g. x¹⁰⁰ + 1 is a binomial of degree 100). B is false: a degree-1 polynomial has at most 2 terms (ax + b).","section":"logical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"If x + 1/x = 4, then the value of x⁴ + 1/x⁴ is:","options":["194","196","1154","14"],"correct":0,"explanation":"x + 1/x = 4 → x² + 1/x² = 16 − 2 = 14. Squaring again: x⁴ + 1/x⁴ = 14² − 2 = 196 − 2 = 194.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"hard"},{"q":"If x² − 1 is a factor of ax⁴ + bx³ + cx² + dx + e, which relation holds?","options":["a + c + e = b + d","a + b + c = d + e","a + c = b + d + e","a + e = b + c + d"],"correct":0,"explanation":"x = 1 and x = −1 are roots. p(1) = a + b + c + d + e = 0 and p(−1) = a − b + c − d + e = 0; adding/subtracting gives a + c + e = b + d.","section":"achievers","difficulty":"hard"},{"q":"For a circular ring, the area depends on (R² − r²). If R = 101 m and r = 99 m, find R² − r² without squaring.","options":["200","400","4000","100"],"correct":1,"explanation":"R² − r² = (R − r)(R + r) = (101 − 99)(101 + 99) = 2 × 200 = 400.","section":"everyday-math","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"A metal sheet of dimensions (x + 5) by (x − 5) has area:","options":["x² − 25","x² + 25","x² − 10x + 25","x² − 5"],"correct":0,"explanation":"(x + 5)(x − 5) = x² − 25 by the identity (a + b)(a − b) = a² − b².","section":"everyday-math","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"What is the degree of the zero polynomial?","options":["0","1","Any natural number","Not defined"],"correct":3,"explanation":"A non-zero constant polynomial has degree 0, but the degree of the zero polynomial is not defined.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"Using Pascal's Triangle, what is the sum of the coefficients in the expansion of (x + y)⁵?","options":["16","25","32","64"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Put x = 1 and y = 1: (1 + 1)⁵ = 2⁵ = 32.","section":"logical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"The factorisation of x² − 5x − 6 is:","options":["(x − 6)(x + 1)","(x − 3)(x − 2)","(x + 6)(x − 1)","(x − 5)(x + 1)"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Split the middle term: x² − 6x + x − 6 = x(x − 6) + 1(x − 6) = (x − 6)(x + 1).","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"If both (x + 1) and (x − 1) are factors of ax³ + x² − 2x + b, find a and b.","options":["a = 2, b = −1","a = −2, b = 1","a = 2, b = 1","a = 1, b = 2"],"correct":0,"explanation":"p(−1) = −a + 1 + 2 + b = 0 → −a + b = −3; p(1) = a + 1 − 2 + b = 0 → a + b = 1. Solving gives b = −1 and a = 2.","section":"achievers","difficulty":"hard"},{"q":"Match each polynomial to its type — (P) 3x² + 5x, (Q) 7x³, (R) 5x + 2 — with (i) Quadratic Binomial, (ii) Cubic Monomial, (iii) Linear Binomial:","options":["P-i, Q-ii, R-iii","P-ii, Q-i, R-iii","P-iii, Q-ii, R-i","P-i, Q-iii, R-ii"],"correct":0,"explanation":"3x² + 5x is a quadratic binomial, 7x³ is a cubic monomial, and 5x + 2 is a linear binomial.","section":"logical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"If a² + b² + c² = 250 and ab + bc + ca = 3, find |a + b + c|.","options":["16","256","14","20"],"correct":0,"explanation":"(a + b + c)² = 250 + 2(3) = 256, so |a + b + c| = √256 = 16.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"To find 249² − 248² quickly, which identity helps, and what is the value?","options":["497","1","495","499"],"correct":0,"explanation":"Using a² − b² = (a − b)(a + b): 249² − 248² = (249 − 248)(249 + 248) = 1 × 497 = 497.","section":"everyday-math","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"In the sequence P₁(x) = x − 1, P₂(x) = x² − 1, P₃(x) = x³ − 1, …, the common linear factor of every term is:","options":["x + 1","x − 1","x","None of these"],"correct":1,"explanation":"For any xⁿ − 1, substituting x = 1 gives 0, so (x − 1) is a factor of every term.","section":"logical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"If p(x) = x + 4, then p(x) + p(−x) is equal to:","options":["0","2x","8","4"],"correct":2,"explanation":"p(x) = x + 4 and p(−x) = −x + 4, so their sum is (x + 4) + (−x + 4) = 8.","section":"mathematical-reasoning","difficulty":"easy"}]}}}